<chapter>

<title><classname>HttpdFile</classname> Reference</title>
 <section id="fsFile" xreflabel="file"><title>Introduction</title>
  
  <para>
   An <classname>HttpdFile</classname> object represents a valid file
   <quote>handle</quote> suitable for performing
   <acronym>I/O</acronym> operations on.  Its semantics are as
   consistent as possible across heterogenous platforms, and this
   class should be used to perform file-related tasks in a portable
   manner.
  </para>

 </section>

 <section><title>Public Methods</title>

  <section><title><function>Read</function></title>
   <para>
    <funcsynopsis>
     <funcprototype>
      <funcdef>
       int
       <function><classname>HttpdFile</classname>::Read</function>
      </funcdef>
      <paramdef>void *<parameter>p_buffer</parameter></paramdef>
      <paramdef>size_t &amp;<parameter>sz</parameter></paramdef>
     </funcprototype>
    </funcsynopsis>
   </para>

   <para>
    Read <parameter class=function>sz</parameter> bytes
    from the parent <classname>HttpdFile</classname> object, and store
    the result in the storage pointed to by <parameter
    class=function>p_buffer</parameter>.
   </para>

   <para>
    Upon success, <literal>0</literal> is returned; otherwise a system
    dependent error value is returned (see <xref
    linkend="opsErrorCodes">).  <parameter
    class=function>sz</parameter> is updated to reflect the actual
    number of bytes read.  If end-of-file is reached, success is
    returned and <parameter class=function>sz</parameter> is set to
    <literal>0</literal>.
   </para>

  </section>

  <section><title><function>Write</function></title>
   <para>
    <funcsynopsis>
     <funcprototype>
      <funcdef>
       int
       <function><classname>HttpdFile</classname>::Write</function>
      </funcdef>
      <paramdef>const void *<parameter>p_buffer</parameter></paramdef>
      <paramdef>size_t <parameter>sz</parameter></paramdef>
     </funcprototype>
    </funcsynopsis>
   </para>

   <para>
    Write <parameter class=function>sz</parameter> bytes from the
    storage pointed to by <parameter
    class=function>p_buffer</parameter> to the parent
    <classname>HttpdFile</classname> object.
   </para>

   <para>
    Upon success, <literal>0</literal> is returned; otherwise a system
    dependent error value is returned (see <xref
    linkend="opsErrorCodes">).  If successful, all bytes were written
    by <function>Write()</function>.
   </para>

  </section>

  <section><title><function>Seek</function></title>
   <para>
    <funcsynopsis>
     <funcprototype>
      <funcdef>
       int
       <function><classname>HttpdFile</classname>::Seek</function>
      </funcdef>
      <paramdef>long <parameter>offset</parameter></paramdef>
      <paramdef>int <parameter>whence</parameter></paramdef>
     </funcprototype>
    </funcsynopsis>
   </para>

   <para>
    Change the current position of the seek pointer associated with
    the parent <classname>HttpdFile</classname>.  If <parameter
    class=function>whence</parameter> is set to
    <constant>FILE_SEEK_START</constant>, <parameter
    class=function>offset</parameter> represents the new absolute
    position of the seek pointer.  A value of
    <constant>FILE_SEEK_CUR</constant> adds <parameter
    class=function>offset</parameter> to the seek pointer's current
    position.  <constant>FILE_SEEK_END</constant> adds <parameter
    class=function>offset</parameter> to the size of the file and sets
    the seek pointer to that value.
   </para>

   <para>
    Upon success, <literal>0</literal> is returned; otherwise a system
    dependent error value is returned (see <xref
    linkend="opsErrorCodes">).
   </para>

  </section>

 </section>

 <section><title>Public Data</title>

  <para>
   Other than the constants mentioned in the
   <function>Seek()</function> entry, <classname>HttpdFile</classname>
   contains no publically available data members.
  </para>

 </section>

</chapter>

